        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Luke 15:3",
        "book": "Luke",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "What man of you, having an hundred sheep, if he lose one of them, doth not leave the ninety and nine in the wilderness, and go after that which is lost, until he find it?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "JST Luke 15:4 … and go into the wilderness after that which is lost …"
          },
          {
            "start": 147,
            "end": 151,
            "text": "Ezek. 34:16 (11–12, 16)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Luke 15:4",
        "book": "Luke",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And when he hath found it, he layeth it on his shoulders, rejoicing.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
